  "summary_en": "Law-faculty article using a feminist phenomenological lens to assess sex robot regulation. It rejects an outright ban, doubts law's suitability for technologies with uncertain outcomes, and evaluates the EU AI Act and soft-law tools such as codes of conduct and design guidelines. It also considers non-anthropomorphic sex robot designs.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Rejects an outright ban on sex robots as grounded in perceived morality.",
   "Sex robots are gendered technology, mostly hyper-sexualised female forms that reinforce patriarchal expectations.",
   "Favours differentiated regulation through soft law: codes of conduct and design guidelines under the EU AI Act.",
   "Questions the suitability of law for technologies with uncertain outcomes.",
   "Proposes non-human-form 'indetermined' sex robot designs to loosen gender binaries."
